api_contract:
- POST /v1/optimize/applies/propose -> returns {apply_token, changeset_id, validation_issues, estimated_cost_delta, fence_id}
- POST /v1/optimize/applies/commit -> body {apply_token} -> returns {status: committed | already_committed}
- POST /v1/optimize/applies/rollback -> body {apply_token | changeset_id} -> returns {status: rolled_back | not_found}
- GET /v1/optimize/applies/{changeset_id} -> returns current state and event log
- Webhook: /webhooks/optimize/execute receives {changeset_id, fence_id, callback_url, requested_action: commit|rollback, signature}
Important: apply_token is timebound and single-use for commit. fence_id is used for leader-election style fencing on distributed executors.
